  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Kiran Rajkumar Mane vs The State Of Maharashtra on 14 October, 2021 Author: Revati Mohite Dere Bench: Revati Mohite Dere Digitally signed by Shagufta Shagufta Q Pathan Q Pathan Date: 8-Ba-349 2021.10.14 16:25:51 +0530 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Criminal Bail Application No. 3494 Of 2021 Kiran Rajkumar Mane ...Applicant Versus The State of Maharashtra ...Respondent Mr. V. V. Purwant a/w Mr. Rushikesh Kale for the Applicant Mr. A. A. Palkar, A.P.P for the Respondent-State Coram : Revati Mohite Dere, J. Thursday, 14th October 2021 P.C. : 1 Heard learned counsel for the parties. 2 By this application, the applicant seeks his enlargement in connection with C.R. No. 570/2021 registered with the Pandharpur Taluka Police Station, Solapur, for the alleged offences punishable u Sections 328, 188, 272, 273 of the Indian Penal Code and under Sectio 26(2)(i), 26(2)(iv), 27(3)(e), 59 r/w 3(1)(zz)(iii) of Food Safety an Standards Act.",
    "facts": "2 By this application, the applicant seeks his enlargement in connection with C.R. No. 570/2021 registered with the Pandharpur Taluka Police Station, Solapur, for the alleged offences punishable u Sections 328, 188, 272, 273 of the Indian Penal Code and under Sectio 26(2)(i), 26(2)(iv), 27(3)(e), 59 r/w 3(1)(zz)(iii) of Food Safety an Standards Act. According to the complainant-Bharath Bhosale, the Foods Safety Officer, Food and Drugs Department, Solapur SQ Pathan 8-BA-3494-2021. on 8th September 2021, he along with the police staff, visited Shriman Paan Shop at Sargam Chowk, Pandharpur, Solapur. In the search that was carried out, paan masala and supari worth Rs. 2,739/- was seized. The applicant is stated to be the owner of the said Shriman Paan Shop. 4 an offence under Section 328 is disclosed qua the applicant",
    "arguments": "",
